<body>
    <h1>Time Control</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<p>The =E2=80=9CTime Control=E2=80=9D panel serves as a key decision-making=
 point within your Logic flow, allowing you to set schedule-based exit path=
s that determine different outcomes based on the timing of input through th=
e panel. This is ideal for handling time-sensitive scenarios, adapting resp=
onses or processes depending on specific days and times.</p>
<p>The panel is configured by creating "events," each representing a custom=
 time period linked to an exit path. You can set up these events as weekly =
recurrences or one-time occurrences, tailoring them to your scheduling need=
s.</p>
<p>Each Time Control panel supports up to ten (10) custom events, providing=
 ten unique exit paths in addition to a default path for non-scheduled time=
s.</p>
<p>With the Time Control panel, you can effectively route interactions base=
d on time-specific conditions to ensure seamless, schedule-aware workflow m=
anagement.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-=
wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-=
image image-center" width=3D"363" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"96104f7333088616f=
d7edf4efc06c80e9e3bcb81b5185b98e20d7327fb049080" data-image-src=3D"https://=
sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/4236312615/Screenshot%202=
024-10-25%20at%202.40.32%E2%80%AFPM.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D=
1729892441985&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"115" data-w=
idth=3D"537" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D=
"4237000706" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=
=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"Screenshot 2024-10-25=
 at 2.40.32=E2=80=AFPM.png" data-base-url=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.ne=
t/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resourc=
e-container-id=3D"4236312615" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"4" =
data-media-id=3D"03958164-2c3e-4f6c-bcc5-05548c7dd35b" data-media-type=3D"f=
ile" height=3D"77"></span>
<h3 id=3D"TimeControl-Usingthispanel">Using this panel</h3>
<p>Situations that require different responses depending on the time are go=
od matches for the Time Control panel. One example would be a business that=
 needs to route customer interactions differently during business hours and=
 after closing for the day.</p>
<h3 id=3D"TimeControl-Configuration">Configuration</h3>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Set as Flow Initiator</strong>: By selecting "Set as Flow Initia=
tor," this panel will serve as the starting point of the IVR flow, before p=
roceeding to subsequent panels within the Logic+ flow.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel Name</strong>: It is recommended that you choose a name an=
d keep it consistent. You will also need to specify the variable name to up=
date. If the variable does not exist, it will be created.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel Description</strong>: It is recommended to provide a clear=
 description of the panel, detailing its purpose and functionality. This is=
 akin to documentation, making it easier for others to understand and ident=
ify its intended use when they encounter it.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Time Zone</strong>: Choose the time zone that best aligns with y=
our IVR flow or organizational requirements.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Use Dropdown:</strong> Select an option from the dropdown menu.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Use Variable:</strong> Input a variable to assign a specific tim=
e zone for each interaction. Based on the path, configuration, or lookup se=
ttings, the variable can dynamically adjust the time zone applied.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Events: </strong>Select the type of event to create by selecting=
 either <strong>Add Weekly Repeating</strong> or <strong>Add One Time Event=
</strong>.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Add Weekly Repeating:</strong> Select the days of the week and s=
pecify a start and end time for each day.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><em>Name:</em> Enter a unique name for the event. Its exit path will sha=
re this name.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Days of the Week:</em> Select one or more day(s) for the event from =
<code>SUN, MON, TUE, WED, THU, FRI,</code> and <code>SAT</code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Time Range:</em> Enter a start and end time for the event. Enter tim=
es as <code>HH:MM:AM/PM</code> in either 12-hour or 24-hour format. 24-hour=
 entries will be converted to 12-hour.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Add One Time Event:</strong> Ideal for single occurrences, such =
as holidays or team meetings. Assign a name, and choose the start date and =
time.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><em>Name:</em> Enter a unique name for the event. Its exit path will sha=
re this name.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Start Date and Time:</em> Enter a starting date and time for the eve=
nt. Enter dates as <code>MM/DD/YYYY</code> and times as <code>HH:MM:AM/PM</=
code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>End Date and Time:</em> Enter an ending date and time for the event.=
 Enter dates as <code>MM/DD/YYYY</code> and times as <code>HH:MM:AM/PM</cod=
e>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Repeat Annually:</em> Turn this toggle on to make this event repeat =
annually. Default setting is off.</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Exit Paths:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Default</strong>: If none of the matches evaluates to true for t=
he provided variable, the default exit path is used.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Custom Added Matches</strong>: Any exit paths created for added =
matches that evaluate to true.</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
